    "result_text": "All tests pass \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`, 17 tests, 0 failures.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `customerCode` assignment (`<LAST3>-<NNNN>`) for `POST /api/owners`.\n\n**New pipeline step** \u2014 `AssignCustomerCode.java`, wired into `owners.POST.yml` between `build` and `save`:\n```java\nString last3 = lastName.substring(0, Math.min(3, lastName.length())).toUpperCase();\nint sequence = ownerRepository.findAll().size() + 1;\nowner.setCustomerCode(String.format(\"%s-%04d\", last3, sequence));\n```\nRunning it before `save` means the count excludes the not-yet-persisted owner, so successive creates increment by one (the global sequence the test asserts). It reads `@Val Owner` and mutates in place, under `govern: [ transaction ]` like the other steps.\n\n**Persistence & serialization** (so `GET /api/owners/{id}` reads the snapshot back):\n- `Owner` entity \u2014 new `customerCode` field mapped to `customer_code` column, plus getter/setter.\n- `customer_code` column added to all four `schema.sql` files (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres), and the column-less seed inserts in `hsqldb`/`mysql` `data.sql` padded with a trailing `NULL`.\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added a read-only `customerCode` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct maps it automatically (by name) in `toOwnerDto`.\n\nThe existing `OwnerMapper` needed no explicit rule since the field name matches on both sides.",
